KG42.register("clusters-4c098d88a4e7c69df9a20c35",{"id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v142-d-CL002","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","label":"Price boundaries for bilateral participation and the external grid option","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"Price boundaries for bilateral participation and the external grid option","market_meaning":"Assemble the buyer's price ceiling and the seller's price floor including FiT and transaction costs with both parties' free trading and the seller's option to sell surplus energy, expressing the price conditions required to maintain bilateral participation. The joint interval in R008 is the pricing-side expression of these boundaries and is not counted as a separate independent participation rule.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation","pricing","activation"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"Use the seller lower bound including transaction costs in the detailed model of 4.1, retain the overview difference that 2.3 writes only FiT, and do not deem the two formulations completely equivalent. The correspondence between TLOU and the actual or marginal grid electricity purchase price remains undetermined; the clause prohibiting simultaneous buying and selling maintains the 5.1 price-setting scope.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The participation conditions of both parties jointly constrain the same bilateral price, and grid transactions provide an external option, carrying independent implications for continuing participation or withdrawal. Here, the pricing output and the duplicated execution-side clause are cited, without re-assuming functions of equilibrium solving, energy-storage dispatch, or fee allocation.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the buyer's price ceiling for continued participation and the permission for free trading."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the seller's participation price floor, the option to sell surplus to the grid, and transaction restrictions that retain the source scope."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provide the pricing-side reference to the same endogenous price and joint boundary; the joint interval does not serve as a newly added independent participation rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"alternative","rationale":"Compare with the execution-side formulation of the seller clause prohibiting simultaneous buying and selling; the buyer's grid energy-purchase content is used only to check the external electricity-price interface, and its primary attribution remains in the transaction-clearing Rule-Cluster."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x-rho-sb-t"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-V-rho"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e04"],"rationale":"The same passage of citation explains the two sides of the boundary of the same bilateral price through buyer and seller withdrawal respectively; the two are complementary, cannot replace each other, and it has not yet been proven that the feasible interval is non-empty."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-rho"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x-rho-sb-t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e04"],"rationale":"The upper side of the joint pricing interval corresponds to the buyer withdrawal condition; here only a partial-scope correspondence is established, and the complete interval is not judged to be the same expression as the one-sided constraint."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-sell","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-cost"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-T-lambda_sell","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-T-lambda_cost"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g03-e04"],"rationale":"The lower side of the joint interval and the seller withdrawal condition use the same FiT and transaction-cost composition; the complete interval and the one-sided participation condition retain different constraint identities."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040"],"rationale":"Both express the prohibition condition that, under the same price-setting situation, the seller must not simultaneously purchase energy from the grid and sell energy to P2P; duplicated references on the execution side and the participation side do not increase the number of independent rules."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e04"],"rationale":"The buyer and seller participation conditions and the joint interval target the same local P2P pricing function; this display-level grouping does not merge the participation nodes or condition edges of the two parties."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M002","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x-rho-sb-t","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-V-rho","v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-x-rho"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e024","v141-b-g03-e04"],"rationale":"The citation explicitly states that the same bilateral P2P price is subject to the withdrawal boundaries of both parties and is generated by equilibrium; the local objects and roles of the buyer condition, seller condition, and overall pricing are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-TLOU","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-TLOU"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e04"],"rationale":"Both places come from the same buyer withdrawal ceiling and both retain the unindexed TLOU; this association does not extend to identity equivalence with the R004 grid electricity price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-T-lambda_sell","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-sell"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g03-e04"],"rationale":"The FiT for the same time period serves respectively as a component of the seller participation lower bound and a component of the joint price interval; each local parameter reference remains independent."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-T-lambda_cost","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-lambda-cost"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g03-e04"],"rationale":"The same P2P transaction cost is used in the detailed seller participation condition and the joint pricing interval, retaining its different local uses."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M006","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C005"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040"],"rationale":"The two clauses are consistent in subject, simultaneous purchase-and-sale activity, prohibited content, and applicable price-setting scope, so one procedural clause may be selected as a display representative; the basis is the same obligation content rather than an empty mathematical expression or shared evidence itself, and both original clauses are retained."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"The participation boundaries, grid option, and duplicated restriction rely on unaudited B evidence; this Rule-Cluster does not mean that the transcription or scientific interpretation has received independent recognition.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g03-e04"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the withdrawal conditions, external transaction options, and test price-setting restrictions in the source text, maintaining the current unverified status until a separate audit."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G002","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The buyer and time-period indices of the TLOU ceiling, the quantifiers over each bilateral price, and its correspondence to the actual or marginal grid electricity purchase price are all unspecified. It cannot be merged with the R004 electricity-price parameter merely because both are electricity prices.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R008","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-TLOU","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-TLOU","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-lambda_buy"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e016","v141-b-g03-e04"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-X03"],"required_work":"Supplement the source definition and applicable quantifiers, clarify the external electricity-price convention, and handle the pending proposal; currently only associate the same unindexed ceiling in the two places."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G003","category":"math_incomplete","description":"If TLOU is interpreted as the actual price priced by purchased quantity in equation (7), then when the grid energy-purchase quantity and coefficient are both positive, the marginal energy-purchase price given by equations (32)–(34) will be higher than that price. The separate setting in which TLOU is higher than FiT is also insufficient by itself to guarantee the feasibility of the lower bound including transaction costs; the existing Rule-Chain has not proven that the price formula and the boundaries of both parties can be satisfied simultaneously.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-lambda_buy","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e040","v141-b-g03-e04","v141-b-g03-e13"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check whether the ceiling means an actual electricity price or marginal cost, and check the jointly feasible conditions of the two parties' boundaries, and complete the corresponding upstream relationships; do not revise the frozen boundaries or equilibrium price formula on one's own."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G004","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The duplicated seller clause prohibiting simultaneous buying and selling has only a procedural formulation; the frozen catalog has no symbol or domain for the seller's grid energy-purchase decision, so its algebraic prohibition condition cannot be formed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e040"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If the source text defines the relevant seller energy-purchase quantity, upstream should record it and then formalize it; otherwise, retain the procedural prohibition within that test scope and do not add variables."}]},"rule_refs":["49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R006","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R007","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R008","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R004"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-3cc1c6ed2324280e","COMP-4c1817f6cddf8a9c","COMP-58a3c8caf66a5d40","COMP-820ecd8f4d709ac7","COMP-a774da994c2ca212","COMP-d3fb5a9d87fcd5a7"]});
